Interesting, 21Shares launched an Anthropic Synthetic ETP in Europe today, first 100% exposure to a private co or cos. Ticker $CLAU. To get the exposure they use total returns swaps on the Kaiko Anthropic USD Reference Rate which is derived from Binance's Anthropic perpetual futures. Prob no one in Europe will care but if they can figure out how to do this in the US (or some Asian countries) look out..

Defiance has an ETF filed that is similar, using swaps that are linked to perps that track the private cos. https://t.co/bVfpJdfTiq

@DaveNadig I’m talking 100% private co tho.  MN is part only right?

@DaveNadig Yes but this one on Europe is 100% swap perp

@DaveNadig Yes ETN, but still interesting as ginnea pig à la btc etns from 2015

$FRMI +20%, announces credit support agreement with AMD supporting a lease for phase 1 of Fermi's Project Matador, 222MW

$CIFR -10%, $850M convertible bond to support Barber Lake capex, upsizeable to $1B. (Why didn't they do this when stock was at $17?)

@CK_Cryptoklepto book value is irrelevant for CIFR at the moment. leases are not on the balance sheet at market value.

@CK_Cryptoklepto If you're asking if the stock should be up on this news, obviously not.
That said, many private companies have lost access to capital markets entirely but CIFR is going to get ~$1B w/ zero cash outlay to build BTM at Barber Lake. Stock will be much higher after the site leased.

@Atzaran3 about half the stocks in this sector have not issued equity since 2025, instead using project level debt financing. the other half have.

@CK_Cryptoklepto Book value is historical cost, so 9x tells you nothing about whether the stock is expensive relative to contracted lease cash flows, and the same logic that makes P/B useless for valuation makes it useless as a trigger for issuing equity.

@theJAXES @CK_Cryptoklepto I just bought some at $10.88 to try to keep position flat. Company said equity would only be necessary if company signed a very large lease (hundreds of MW up to GW).
Sounds like that's coming. Call at 10:30am.

@theJAXES @CK_Cryptoklepto Actually this is to pay for the cost over-runs at Barber Lake which they are splitting with the tenant. We estimate a double-digit unlevered yield on this extra spend.

